# Survey – generated by the "question‑me" skill

## Round 1

This round clarifies your runner Restart / Update request in plain, non-technical language. The screenshot you shared shows one runner row ("local-alpha") with PAUSE / REVOKE / RELOAD buttons, a line about which build it was made from, and a yellow warning that its version does not match the main system.

```survey-json
{
  "round": 1,
  "generatedAt": "2026-11-16T20:48:53.000Z",
  "stage": "question-me",
  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "q1",
      "type": "single",
      "text": "You asked for RESTART and UPDATE as two separate buttons instead of the current RELOAD. What should each button do?",
      "options": [
        "Restart = reboot the runner on its current version, Update = reinstall it onto a different/newer version (Recommended)",
        "Restart = stop and start the runner again, Update = check the version and reinstall only if it is out of date",
        "Something else (please explain in Notes)"
      ],
      "required": true,
      "showIf": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q2",
      "type": "single",
      "text": "You want Restart marked as a destructive action with a confirmation window first. What should that confirmation window tell you?",
      "options": [
        "Warn that any work currently running on that runner will be stopped (Recommended)",
        "Warn that the runner will go offline briefly and then come back",
        "Just a simple 'Are you sure?' with no extra detail"
      ],
      "required": true,
      "showIf": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q3",
      "type": "single",
      "text": "You want each runner to have a version setting: either one fixed version or 'Latest' (with 'Latest' as the default). How should that setting look?",
      "options": [
        "A dropdown on each runner showing 'Latest' plus every released version to pick from (Recommended)",
        "Only two choices: 'Latest' or 'Stay on the current version'",
        "One global 'Latest or fixed' switch that applies to all runners at once"
      ],
      "required": true,
      "showIf": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q4",
      "type": "single",
      "text": "When the runner's version does not match what it should be, you want a warning with an Update button. When should that warning appear?",
      "options": [
        "Whenever the runner's version differs from its own setting, whether it is fixed or 'Latest' (Recommended)",
        "Only when it is set to 'Latest' and a brand-new version has been published",
        "Only when it is set to a fixed version and it is not actually running that version"
      ],
      "required": true,
      "showIf": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q5",
      "type": "single",
      "text": "You said only runners set to 'Latest' should ever update themselves automatically. When should that automatic update happen?",
      "options": [
        "Automatically, as soon as a new version is published (Recommended)",
        "Only when the runner next restarts or is sitting idle with no work running",
        "Never fully automatic — always show the Update button and let me click it"
      ],
      "required": true,
      "showIf": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q6",
      "type": "single",
      "text": "You want a scary red warning when a newer version exists so people feel pushed to update. When should the warning turn red?",
      "options": [
        "Red when a newer version exists than the one the runner is on, softer colour for other mismatches (Recommended)",
        "Red for every kind of version mismatch, no softer level",
        "Red only for runners set to 'Latest' that have fallen behind"
      ],
      "required": true,
      "showIf": null
    }
  ],
  "answers": {
    "q1": {
      "selected": [
        "Restart = reboot the runner on its current version, Update = reinstall it onto a different/newer version (Recommended)"
      ],
      "notes": "restart may be used if a runner looks stuck as a debug"
    },
    "q2": {
      "selected": [
        "Warn that any work currently running on that runner will be stopped (Recommended)"
      ],
      "notes": ""
    },
    "q3": {
      "selected": [
        "A dropdown on each runner showing 'Latest' plus every released version to pick from (Recommended)"
      ],
      "notes": ""
    },
    "q4": {
      "selected": [
        "Whenever the runner's version differs from its own setting, whether it is fixed or 'Latest' (Recommended)"
      ],
      "notes": ""
    },
    "q5": {
      "selected": [
        "Only when the runner next restarts or is sitting idle with no work running"
      ],
      "notes": ""
    },
    "q6": {
      "selected": [
        "Red when a newer version exists than the one the runner is on, softer colour for other mismatches (Recommended)"
      ],
      "notes": ""
    }
  }
}
```

